From: Rayek <Rayekkk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] color: scale Gamma 2.2 SDR white only with HDR content

A Gamma 2.2 HDR-capable output can remain enabled while gamescope is
compositing only SDR content. In that state there is no HDR headroom to
reserve, and applying the SDR-on-HDR white scale unnecessarily limits the
entire SDR frame.

Use gamescope's existing focused-app HDR signal to gate the traditional-HDR
scale. The resulting boolean already participates in LUT cache currentness,
so entering or leaving HDR content rebuilds the LUTs with the appropriate
gain.

diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -159,6 +159,7 @@ static lut3d_t g_tmpLut3d;
 extern int g_nDynamicRefreshHz;
 
 bool g_bForceHDRSupportDebug = false;
+extern bool g_bAppWantsHDRCached;
 extern float g_flInternalDisplayBrightnessNits;
 extern float g_flHDRItmSdrNits;
 extern float g_flHDRItmTargetNits;
@@ -482,7 +483,10 @@ update_color_mgmt()
 	if ( !GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector() )
 		return;
 
+	// The output can stay in HDR while only SDR content is being composited.
+	// Reserve SDR headroom only when the base layer actually requests HDR.
 	const bool bTraditionalHDROutput = g_bOutputHDREnabled &&
+		g_bAppWantsHDRCached &&
 		GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetHDRInfo().IsHDRG22();
 
 	GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetNativeColorimetry(
